 Based on your instructions and the provided JSON data, I have converted it into a valid Turtle file using Records in Context Ontology (RiC-O). Please find the conversion below:

```turtle
@prefix rico: <https://www.ica.org/standards/RiC/ontology#> .

<_001> a rico:RecordResource ;
   rico:title "University of Lleida Budget Report 2020" ;
   rico:isAssociatedWithDate <_date_2020> .

<_income> a rico:Event ;
   rico:hasAgent <_stateAuthorities>, <_localAuthorities>, <_students>, <_grantScholarships> , <_investments> ;
   rico:eventType "Income" .

<_expenditure> a rico:Event ;
   rico:hasAgent <_personnel>, <_goodsServices>, <_investments>, <_governmentEntities> ;
   rico:eventType "Expenditure" ;
   rico:amount [rico:value "Decreased by nearly 46%"] .

<_programs> a rico:Activity ;
   rico:hasParticipant <_students>, <_undergraduatePrograms>, <_postgraduatePrograms> ;
   rico:eventType "Scholarships and Grants" .

<_challenges> a rico:Event ;
   rico:hasAgent <_governmentOfCatalonia>, <_universitySystem> ;
   rico:eventType "Lack of Funding Model Application".

<_rectorStatement> a rico:RecordPart ;
   rico:isCreatorOf <_001> ;
   rico:title "Concern about Lack of Funding Model and Quality of Education" .

# Dates, agents, programs, etc. are assumed to be defined elsewhere in the Turtle file for brevity.
```
In this conversion, `_001` represents the University of Lleida Budget Report 2020, `_income`, `_expenditure`, and `_programs` represent their respective sections in the report, and `_challenges` and `_rectorStatement` represent specific points mentioned in the report. The relations between these entities are defined using RiC-O properties such as `rico:isAssociatedWithDate`, `rico:hasAgent`, `rico:eventType`, `rico:amount`, `rico:hasParticipant`, and `rico:isCreatorOf`.